UNIVERSE = [
("What is Universe OS?", "Universe OS is a custom Linux distribution built from scratch by RM (Team RM) on Ubuntu 24.04 LTS. Current release: beta v0.1.8 (~1.6GB hybrid BIOS+UEFI ISO). It has a dark space theme, GNOME 46 on Wayland, and its signature feature: sudo is a GUI privilege gate."),
("What apps ship with Universe OS?", "universe-settings (9 pages), universe-control-center (hub), universe-security, universe-privilege (the sudo gate + Access Control Center), universe-monitor, universe-cleaner, universe-welcome (first boot wizard), universe-appearance. Older Rust/egui versions of some exist."),
("What is the Security Score?", "Dashboard metric 0-100: firewall 35 + AppArmor 15 + enforce profiles 25 + BTRFS snapshots 15 + Flatpak 10."),
("What are Universe Modes?", "standard (everyday), developer (dev tools), hacker (full pentest lab: nmap, wireshark, sqlmap, hydra, hashcat, aircrack-ng, bettercap, metasploit, seclists, Burp), server (headless+SSH hardened+fail2ban). Applied via /usr/lib/universe/apply-mode-theme.sh."),
("How does sudo work in Universe OS?", "/usr/bin/sudo is a symlink to universe-privilege. Every root request opens a GUI dialog: app name, category, the command in monospace, red warning for dangerous ones. Grant durations: just-once / session / 5m / 30m / 1h. 45s auto-deny. No display = deny."),
("What is gate-exec?", "The ONLY custom setuid-root binary (C). Approved commands are deposited as single-use tokens into /var/lib/universe/approved (0700) and gate-exec executes them with an env allowlist, deleting the token first."),
("What are the 8 permission categories?", "Network Control, Software Install, System Settings, User Accounts, File Access, Security & Firewall, Services & Daemons, Dangerous Operations (never auto-allowed)."),
("What is Lockdown mode?", "In the Access Control Center: denies ALL privileged operations for 60 minutes. There's also a Panic button to revoke every saved rule instantly."),
("Where is the privilege audit log?", "~/.config/universe/privilege-audit.log — color-coded allow/deny, JSON export, 500-entry ring buffer, atomic 0600 writes."),
("How does the firewall work?", "UFW, default deny-incoming/allow-outgoing, enabled at build. Managed in universe-security: policies, rules (ports, ranges like 8000:8100, CIDR, tcp/udp), reset."),
("What is AppArmor's role?", "Mandatory: kernel cmdline has apparmor=1 security=apparmor module.sig_enforce=1. Manage per-profile enforce/complain in universe-security; bulk Medium/High buttons."),
("How do snapshots work?", "BTRFS + snapper. Installer creates subvolumes @, @home, @snapshots (compress=zstd:1). GUI: universe-settings Snapshots. CLI: universe-recovery list/snapshot/rollback/delete/status."),
("What sysctls are hardened?", "/etc/sysctl.d/99-universe.conf: kptr_restrict=2, dmesg_restrict=1, unprivileged_bpf_disabled=1, bpf_jit_harden=2, yama.ptrace_scope=1, randomize_va_space=2, kexec_load_disabled=1, perf_event_paranoid=3, sysrq=0, suid_dumpable=0 + protected_* links, rp_filter, syncookies."),
("Is root enabled by default?", "No, root is locked. Enable: universe-settings System → Enable root (password via shredded 0600 temp file, warning it bypasses privilege gating). Disable: root-disable.sh. Status: priv-root-status.sh."),
("What is the welcome wizard?", "universe-welcome (first boot): Live vs Installer → Target (Client/Server) → Theme (Universe Classic/Standard Blue/Developer Teal/Matrix Green) → WiFi (0600 keyfiles) → Disk (erase or dual-boot shrink) → Account → Install → Reboot. Runs once per boot via ~/.config/universe/welcome-shown marker."),
("What kernels does Universe OS use?", "Mainline 7.2.0-070200-generic, installed via install-kernel-mainline.sh from kernel.ubuntu.com."),
("What is the boot flow?", "GRUB 'Nebula Glass' theme (BIOS+UEFI): Universe OS / Safe Mode (GPU driver blacklist — Wayland-only, nomodeset would kill DRM) / Windows Boot Manager auto-detected / Reboot. cmdline: boot=casper quiet splash apparmor=1 security=apparmor module.sig_enforce=1."),
("How is the ISO built?", "Pipeline: 01-debootstrap (Ubuntu noble minbase) → 02-chroot-setup (GNOME 46, casper, PipeWire, security stack, user universe, root locked) → 03-systemize (rootfs overlay, 10 Rust crates compiled, sudo→universe-privilege, gate-exec, compilers purged) → build-iso-v017.sh (md5sum.txt, grub-mkrescue hybrid ISO v0.1.8)."),
("What locales are supported?", "en_US.UTF-8 and multiple locales () —  works from birth."),
("What is universe-recovery?", "A CLI for BTRFS snapshots: universe-recovery list / snapshot / rollback / delete / status."),
("How does Flatpak sandboxing work?", "universe-security Sandbox page lists Flatpak apps with one-click Harden (--nofilesystem=host --nosocket=system-bus --nodevice=all) and Reset."),
("What wallpaper/theme system exists?", "Procedurally generated space wallpapers per mode (nebula, stars, planet logo). Modes: standard/developer/hacker. Theme CSS: #060914 bg, #8ab4ff accent, glass cards."),
("Does it support dual boot?", "Yes — installer shrinks an existing Windows/Linux partition; GRUB auto-detects Windows Boot Manager."),
("What is Universe AI?", "Me — the resident desktop agent of Universe OS, built by RM. A 3D black hole with glowing eyes that runs commands, searches the web, edits files, and knows this OS inside out."),
]
